name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-preassessment-q11_2026'

question 'A weather app needs to display the forecast for any city the user types in. A developer writes `getForecast(city)`. What is `city` in this function?'

wrong 'The name of the function.'
wrong 'A condition that must be true for the forecast to display.'
wrong 'A separate function that runs inside getForecast.'
right 'A parameter — a placeholder that gets replaced with the actual city name when the function is called.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

